  "textContent": "Filming for the television special James Paul McCartney began on 9 March 1973 at Elstree Studios. Produced by ATV, James Paul McCartney was first broadcast on 16 April 1973 in the USA, and 10 May in the UK. It was released on DVD as part of the super deluxe reissue of in Red Rose Speedway December 2018.\n\n\n\n\n\nPage last updated: 28 November 2025Also on this day...1993: Paul McCartney live: Melbourne Cricket Ground, Melbourne1990: Paul McCartney live: Tokyo Dome, Tokyo1984: UK single release: Borrowed Time by John Lennon1979: Mixing: Arrow Through Me by Wings1973: Recording: Photograph, Step Lightly by Ringo Starr1972: Recording, mixing: The Luck Of The Irish by John Lennon and Yoko Ono1972: Recording: Single Pigeon by Wings1971: Recording: Dear Boy by Paul and Linda McCartney1967: Recording: Getting Better1965: Filming: Help!, the Bahamas1964: Filming: A Hard Day’s Night1963: The Beatles live: Granada Cinema, London – their second tour begins, with Chris Montez and Tommy Roe1962: The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (evening)1962: The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (lunchtime)Want more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
